title: Avoid RocksDB dependency in subkey build
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: "## Summary\n\nThis changes `subkey` to depend on `sc-cli` without\
    \ default features.\n\n`subkey` reuses the key-related `sc-cli` commands, but\
    \ does not need the default `rocksdb` feature. Keeping that default enabled pulls\
    \ in `librocksdb-sys`, which means a direct `subkey` build can fail on machines\
    \ where the RocksDB build script cannot load `libclang.dylib`.\n\n## Root Cause\n\
    \nThe failing dependency path was:\n\n```text\nsubkey\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 sc-cli\
    \ default feature\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 sc-cli rocksdb feature\n        \u2514\
    \u2500\u2500 sc-client-db/rocksdb\n            \u2514\u2500\u2500 kvdb-rocksdb\n\
    \                \u2514\u2500\u2500 rocksdb\n                    \u2514\u2500\u2500\
    \ librocksdb-sys\n```\n\nThe observed local failure was:\n\n```text\nerror: failed\
    \ to run custom build command for `librocksdb-sys v0.17.3+10.4.2`\n\ndyld: Library\
    \ not loaded: @rpath/libclang.dylib\n```\n\n## Change\n\nUse:\n\n```toml\nsc-cli\
    \ = { workspace = true, default-features = false }\n```\n\nfor `subkey`, avoiding\
    \ the unnecessary RocksDB/native build dependency.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\n\
    SKIP_WASM_BUILD=1 cargo build -p subkey --locked\ncargo tree -p subkey --locked\
    \ -i librocksdb-sys\n```\n\nThe build succeeds, and `librocksdb-sys` is no longer\
    \ present in `subkey`'s dependency graph.\n\n## Release Notes\n\nNo prdoc is included\
    \ because this only narrows an internal build-time dependency for `subkey` and\
    \ should not require crate publication. Please apply `R0-no-crate-publish-required`\
    \ if appropriate."
crates:
- name: subkey
  bump: patch
